[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Requested batch control dispatch

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-CONTROL-BATCHMODE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Select the original root transient in a bounded batch branch
STATEMENT: >>>
For one root transient and a single root control block conditioned on the exact ngspice batchmode existence query, the batch profile shall retain the root transient when the true branch only reports through echo. The unselected interactive branch shall admit only echo, plot, parsed analysis commands and unset ngdebug. Other commands, nested branching and commands outside the envelope shall refuse this profile. Qualification shall omit the entire control block from its isolated projection, retain the exact root transient source, and record the omitted reporting and interactive effects.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
RequestedControlPreparation, OriginalProjection and RequestedBatchControlTests implement and verify this bounded behavior. Both original if-batchmode.cir paths in the pinned ngspice corpus provide execution evidence. Reporting reproduction, interactive execution and transient numerical agreement are separate concerns.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-CONTROL-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-CONTROL-VECTORTYPE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Record terminal power vector type as a reporting omission
STATEMENT: >>>
The requested analysis dispatcher shall admit settype power followed by a single simple device power vector name only in the unbranched terminal reporting region after the last analysis. It shall preserve the omitted plot metadata change in the result and leave analysis preparation and native numerical projection unchanged. Other target shapes, types, separators and dispatch-affecting placements shall be refused.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
ControlPowerVectorType in the generated grammar, ControlExtraction and RequestedControlPreparation implement admission. RequestedPowerVectorTypeTests cover the terminal command, projection and malformed placements. The paranoia_parallel probe-i-dev.cir contains this original reporting command. No plot metadata parity is claimed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEM-CONTROL-001
